{% comment %}
  TRMNL private plugin markup — voice chess board.
  Modeled on the Lichess Daily Puzzle layout: the board is a single remote
  image, so no CSS board and no dithering problems.

  merge_variables pushed by chess_mcp_server.py:
    image_url, status, last_move, move_number, turn, player_color, history,
    engine, level, white_captured, black_captured, white_edge, black_edge

  The board image is oriented to player_color (the user's own pieces at the
  bottom), so it's worth always showing player_color on-screen too -- without
  it, a flipped board with no label is confusing rather than clarifying.

  white_captured/black_captured are Unicode chess glyphs for the pieces
  that side has captured, oldest-value-first (confirmed live: the glyphs
  render correctly on real TRMNL hardware). white_edge/black_edge are the
  material lead ("+3") shown ONLY next to whichever side is ahead -- never
  both, matching Lichess/Chess.com.

  STRUCTURE NOTE: TRMNL's own canonical multi-column example is a single
  top-level .layout wrapping .columns > .column -- NOT a second nested
  .layout inside .layout (an earlier version of this file did that and
  content got clipped off the top/bottom of the fixed 800x480 canvas,
  confirmed via screenshot on real hardware; nesting .layout compounds its
  own intrinsic spacing rather than just adding a flex row). .columns also
  has a built-in overflow engine for exactly this "doesn't fit" case.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="layout">
  <div class="columns">

    <div class="column" style="width: 14%;">
      <span class="label label--small">White</span>
      <span class="label label--base">{{ white_captured }}</span>
      {% if white_edge != "" %}
        <span class="label label--small label--outline">{{ white_edge }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="column">
      <div class="flex flex--row flex--between flex--center-y">
        <span class="label label--base lg:label--large">
          Move {{ move_number }} — {{ turn }} to play
        </span>
        <span class="label label--outline label--base lg:label--large">
          {{ engine }} · {{ level }}
        </span>
      </div>

      <img style="max-width:100%; max-height:70cqh; object-fit:contain;"
           src="{{ image_url }}" alt="Chess board">

      <span class="label label--base lg:label--base">
        {% for move in history %}{{ move }}{% unless forloop.last %} · {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
      </span>
    </div>

    <div class="column" style="width: 14%;">
      <span class="label label--small">Black</span>
      <span class="label label--base">{{ black_captured }}</span>
      {% if black_edge != "" %}
        <span class="label label--small label--outline">{{ black_edge }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  <span class="title">Voice Chess — playing {{ player_color }}</span>
  <span class="instance">{{ last_move }} · {{ status }} · {{ engine }} {{ level }}</span>
</div>
